                <pb facs="0754" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11408: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-02T16:00:00+09:00">December 2, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 2—8:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>588. Department’s 326, December 1, 8 p.m.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>The Department presumably will have noted our 582, November 30, 7 p.m.,
                        (to which reference was made in Shanghai’s 1050, December 1, 11 a.m.<anchor
                            n="70" xml:id="d827-f1"/>) in which case we reported having taken action
                        in anticipation of the Department’s instructions.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Today we informed the Foreign Office of the statement made by the Japanese
                        Assistant Military Attaché at British military headquarters, as reported in
                        Shanghai’s 1057,<anchor n="71" xml:id="d827-f2"/> and again urged against
                        sending of Japanese troops into neutral areas. The Foreign Office stated
                        that according to a report received from Shanghai the project to march
                        Japanese forces into such areas has been “abandoned” and “the question does
                        not arise”.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
